{"entryId":"1389","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1389:1","sourceSha256":"e7fbc2c13fe05ee6d8240e327907fcbaa9c04a99b961f25afd963040dc2266c1","englishSha256":"83ac16be6f1d48459a69c0b50d10ac34d98634636b603f6ed843d6b673578004","citations":[{"id":"1389:1:citation-01","he":[4,14],"en":[7,21],"target":{"entry":4,"paragraph":12},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 4:12","assessment":"The Rav roster gives Abba bar Chana with the other written form and the reciprocal relation to Rav. The roster does not establish that Abba and Rabbah share one individual father.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 4:12","target":{"entry":4,"paragraph":12},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1389:1:citation-02","he":[16,26],"en":[23,39],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_5a.10"},"reference":"Sanhedrin 5a:10","assessment":"The exact Sanhedrin passage names Rabbah bar Chana and attests Chana as his father. No relationship to the Abba heading is inferred.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 5a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_5a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 5a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_5a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The local roster supplies Abba and the exact Sanhedrin passage gives Rabbah. Preserve both forms.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 5a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_5a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 5a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_5a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 4:12","target":{"entry":4,"paragraph":12},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
